# The finish of norm_upper_2 (milestone2.md, "sum, dot, axpy, convolution": norm_upper_k; "When
# something is not finite"): one step up from the largest magnitude of a leading limb, which is at
# least the magnitude of every element (normalized_2_between) and at most one step above the
# smallest number of the format not below the largest of them, when no element was a NaN (the mask
# ok) and that step is finite, with the flag true; otherwise the canonical NaN and the flag false.
# The step from the largest finite number is infinite: an element above it in magnitude gives the
# flag false.
kernel:        norm_finish_2
input:         m
input:         mask ok
output:        r
output:        mask flag
value:         m
ensures:       finite_or_nan r flag=flag if=ok steps=1
min_precision: 1
source:        the finish of a fold of maxima: the step after the maximum, or the canonical NaN (milestone2.md)
license:       proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
cone_exempt:   the outputs are selects after the mask ok and an explicit test that the step up is finite (fold_finish_1), which is what the kernel claims

s         = succ(m)
t         = select(ok, s, const nan)
(r, flag) = fold_finish_1(t)
